      "content": "While you can silence the warning using `pd.options.mode.chained_assignment = None`, this is generally considered a bad practice because it completely hides debugging signals from Pandas. It's much safer to fix the underlying code structure to be explicit, as that's how you guarantee correctness. If you must disable it temporarily for a large block, use a context manager (`with pd.option_context('mode.chained_assignment', None):`) so it only affects that specific section of your notebook.",
